jank: licences

The firmware is GPL-3.0-only, as a whole.
  firmware/, core/, tests/ and scripts/ are licensed under the GNU General Public
  License, version 3 only. This is because the firmware links Optimist's
  fm1base/link/link.c (GPL-3.0-only), a C port of the protocol of Ableton's Link
  library. The whole of the firmware binary is therefore GPL-3.0-only. The full licence
  text is at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt and in Optimist's LICENSES folder.

  core/jank_core.c, the bridge, was written new from the MODE JAM air format and does not
  contain Optimist's wifi_jam.c or wifi_ip.c. tests/crosscheck_optimist.c compiles those
  two files at test time as a check; it is not part of the firmware.

The control page is separate and MIT.
  page/jank.html and tests/test_page.js are under the MIT licence below. The page only
  talks to the stick over a serial port, and contains no code of the firmware.

